Scaffolded from `@aihu/templates-cf-solo` (Aihu __AIHU_VERSION__).

## TL;DR

Cloudflare Workers single-package app with [Aihu](https://github.com/aihu-project/aihu).
Lint/format via Biome, tests via Vitest, agent-discoverable by default.

## Quickstart

```bash
bun install
bun run dev      # local dev server
bun run build    # production bundle
bun run test     # unit tests
bun run check    # biome check + write
```

## Project structure

```
.
├── src/
│   ├── main.ts           # Cloudflare Workers entry
│   ├── aihu-app.aihu      # root SFC, mounted client-side via index.html
│   └── components/       # your components
├── wrangler.toml          # Cloudflare Workers config
├── biome.json              # lint + format
├── tsconfig.json           # TypeScript config
└── .mcp.json                # agent surface (auto-discovered by MCP-aware tools)
```

## Agent surface

If you scaffolded with `agentSurface !== 'none'`, this project ships a
`.mcp.json` at the repo root. MCP-aware editors and CLIs (Claude Code,
Cursor, etc.) auto-discover it and can connect to the Aihu agent host
without further configuration.

To opt out later, delete `.mcp.json` and the `src/agent/aihu-expose.aihu`
file (if present).

## Deploy

GitHub Actions are wired up:
- `ci.yml` — runs on every push and PR (typecheck, test, build)
- `deploy.yml` — runs on push to `main`, deploys via `wrangler deploy`

Set `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` as repo secrets to
enable the deploy workflow.

